  "limits": [
    "The old pin reproduces the title and assignee identifier collision. The current public SDK resolves each field ID before any patch.",
    "The first proposal drops headerless Section selectors. The narrower patch moves metadata to a visible titled header and preserves the observed headerless trees.",
    "The existing Source141 and Source150 authorities refuse either renderer patch. Their seals, pinned consumers and Pair24 tuple were not advanced.",
    "iOS native accessibility and actual task entry and save remain unexecuted. No Simulator or physical-device operations were performed.",
    "The direct XCTest Swift typecheck could not resolve XCTest overlays. The actual Xcode app and XCTest targets built successfully for generic iOS.",
    "The scratch clones, app artifacts, logs and outputs were task-owned. The probe closed each of its own windows and its executable exited."
  ]
